  <title>
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">Tujenge Amani project - Hand in hand for Peace in the Great Lakes Region</narrative>
  </title>
  <description>
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">The Tujenge Amani project, is a two-year peacebuilding initiative designed to foster stability, reconciliation, and good governance in the Great Lakes Region&#x2014;specifically in Burundi, the Democratic Republic of Congo (DRC), and Rwanda. Rooted in the moral authority and cross-border reach of the Catholic Church, the project will seek to empower Church leaders, women and youth to actively engage in non-violent conflict transformation.

By facilitating high-level episcopal advocacy, strengthening community peace networks&#x2014;especially women-led groups&#x2014;and enhancing data collection and monitoring capacity within Justice and Peace Commissions, the project will address the root causes of regional instability. It will also strengthen ACEAC&#x2019;s institutional ability to coordinate and sustain peace efforts across national boundaries.</narrative>
  </description>
